{#
  module/Books/view/books/texts/search-bar.phtml, ported.

  A near-twin of schoenstatt/_contact-search-bar.html.twig and deliberately a separate
  file, because the two differ in three ways that would each need a flag: this one has no
  "Advanced search" link and no `#options` block at all, its default action is `texts`,
  and its `class="row search-bar "` concatenates the centre class **with a leading space**
  (`" search-bar-center"`) where the contact bar's has none. That last one is a one-byte
  difference in the original, and merging the two files would mean either losing it or
  carrying a flag for it.

  The `inLanguage` select the form defines is not rendered here — the .phtml renders only
  the `search` field — and neither is the submit element; the button is hand-written
  markup.

  The commented-out inlineScript block at the foot of the .phtml is not carried over: it
  is commented out, it is JavaScript rather than markup, and an HTML comment is the only
  thing a `.phtml` comment could become. Nothing renders from it on either side.
#}
<div class="row search-bar {% if center_on_page|default(false) %} search-bar-center{% endif %}">
      <div class="col-md-6 col-md-offset-3 col-xs-12">
          <div id="custom-search-input">
            {{ form_open(form, action|default(laminas_path('texts'))) }}
              <div class="input-group col-md-12">
                    {{ form_element(form.get('search')) }}
                  <span class="input-group-btn">
                      <button class="btn btn-info btn-lg" type="submit">
                          <i class="glyphicon glyphicon-search"></i>
                      </button>
                  </span>
              </div>
            {{ form_close() }}
          </div>
      </div>
</div>
